WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.353
- Alright everybody,

00:00:01.353 --> 00:00:02.680
we have hit that part of the show

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:05.230
when I deliver you good
news from the interwebs.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.522
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.522 --> 00:00:07.739
(upbeat keyboard music)

00:00:07.739 --> 00:00:09.925
(audience cheers)

00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:11.474
This story begins when a young girl

00:00:11.474 --> 00:00:12.383
here in Southern California

00:00:12.383 --> 00:00:15.460
discovered that hotels tossed
their linens in the trash

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.630
when there's the smallest imperfection.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.620
Things like pin marks
or lipstick residue -

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.149
lipstick residues, alright.

00:00:23.149 --> 00:00:24.235
(audience laughs)

00:00:24.235 --> 00:00:25.068
Sorry.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.150
So she set out to put
those linens to good use.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.960
She launched a nonprofit that collects

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.590
the gently used bedding and towels,

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.730
and delivers them to
places that can use them,

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.590
including homeless shelters,
veterans organizations,

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.870
and animal shelters.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.210
In the past six years,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.224
she and her hundreds of student volunteers

00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:46.410
have kept more than 45,000
items out of landfills.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.510
Thank you.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.750
From Linens N Love,

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.832
let's say hi to Vivian everybody!

00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:52.728
(audience applauds)

00:00:52.728 --> 00:00:53.561
Hi Vivian!

00:00:55.453 --> 00:00:56.330
- Hi Kelly!

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:57.163
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:57.163 --> 00:00:59.070
First of all - I love your dimple, Vivian,

00:00:59.070 --> 00:00:59.903
and your name.

00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:01.600
That little dimple is adorable.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.060
Tell us more about how
this all got started.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.550
- Yeah, so when I was younger,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.750
my dad worked at a motel near Disneyland

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.670
and my sister and I spent a lot of time

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.780
using the motel linens
to make pillow forts,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.010
or play super competitive
hide and go seek.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.210
So one day my dad told us the
story behind these linens,

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.110
and basically these linens were discarded

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.500
if they don't meet hotel standards.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.930
And even worse,

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.070
they were being sent to landfills

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.180
which is definitely not
good for our environment.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.610
So my sister and I
approached the management

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.650
of different hotels and
they were very, very kind

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.690
to supply us with gently used towels,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.820
blankets, sheets, and even pillows.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.900
So that's basically how
Linens N Love was born.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.525
- [Kelly] That's amazing!

00:01:50.525 --> 00:01:51.965
(audience applauds)

00:01:51.965 --> 00:01:52.798
And it also,

00:01:52.798 --> 00:01:54.470
it's not only helpful for
people that need them,

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.810
but also keeping all that
waste out of landfills.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:57.880
It's just, it's amazing.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.810
It's very eco-friendly, I love it.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.620
This has grown into
something huge though, right?

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.860
- Yeah. Yeah, it has.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.640
It's been very, very exciting.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:09.210
So we started the nonprofit
as just two sisters,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.763
ages 12 and 14,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.520
back in 2014.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.440
But here we are today with
500 student volunteers

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.350
and 35 chapters across 15 countries -

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.270
including here in the US,

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.680
Canada, Singapore, and so much more.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.680
And ultimately our goal is to repurpose

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.070
a hundred thousand linens.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:31.180
And I just- I cannot wait
to see what's to come.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.286
- I love how inspiring you are.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.609
(audience applauds)

00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:35.442
I really want to,

00:02:35.442 --> 00:02:38.570
I want to do a whole show on
just sustainable life tips.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.150
I think that's so incredibly innovative,

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.160
I think it's needed and necessary.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.610
Thank you so much, Vivian,
for sharing your time

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:47.244
and your innovation with us.

00:02:47.244 --> 00:02:48.263
(audience cheers)

00:02:48.263 --> 00:02:49.390
Good luck in college!

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.310
I'm liking your posts right now.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.452
That's not all though.

00:02:52.452 --> 00:02:53.285
- [Vivian] Thank you!

00:02:53.285 --> 00:02:54.118
- Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:54.118 --> 00:02:55.820
the go to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.620
thinks what you're doing
is as inspiring as we do.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:02:59.453
In recognition,

00:02:59.453 --> 00:03:01.070
they'll be using their
Frixion Erasable pen

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.500
to write you a check for a grand.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.020
How's a thousand dollars sound?

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.457
(audience cheers)

